{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/djosh34/tigerstore/pulls/79","id":4840704723,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVGREgM8AAAABIIdK0w","html_url":"https://github.com/djosh34/tigerstore/pull/79","diff_url":"https://github.com/djosh34/tigerstore/pull/79.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/djosh34/tigerstore/pull/79.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/djosh34/tigerstore/issues/79","number":79,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fewer allocations per request on the batch path","user":{"login":"djosh34","id":35622390,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NjIyMzkw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35622390?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34","html_url":"https://github.com/djosh34","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/djosh34/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Part of #50. Stacked on #77; the base becomes `main` as #75, #76 and #77 merge.\n\nThe [benchmark on #75](https://github.com/djosh34/tigerstore/pull/75) measured 34.6 leader allocations per Put on #76 at 256 clients. This PR removes the per-request allocations that the batch path still has in the frontend and the core:\n\n- **Header blocks.** x/net's `ReadMetaHeaders` built a `MetaHeadersFrame` with a fresh field slice for every request: 10 allocations per gRPC header block, measured with `testing.AllocsPerRun` on a grpc-go request. The reader now owns one `hpack.Decoder` whose emit function fills the request's fields directly. Once the fields are in the HPACK dynamic table, which happens from the second request on a connection, a block decodes with 0 allocations; `TestHeaderDecodeAllocs` holds that. The checks x/net made are kept: lowercase token field names, valid values, pseudo-fields first and only the known ones, and a 1 MiB limit on the decoded block. A block that breaks them resets its stream, and the HPACK state stays in step. CONTINUATION frames feed the same decoder; the Framer still checks their order.\n- **Replies.** The Put replies of one completion batch are encoded into one shared buffer, each a clipped slice of it, instead of one buffer each.\n- **Output items.** A stream's output slice starts with room for headers, message and trailers, so a unary reply no longer grows it twice.\n- **Core bookkeeping.** `core.Node.SubmitAll` takes a batch's `pending` records in one allocation; the node driver uses it for `SubmitBatch`.\n\nTests: `go test -race -short` of server, node and core pass locally, 16 simulator seeds pass, and golangci-lint is clean. A Sol helper is benchmarking #77; this PR will get the same comparison.\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T08:46:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T10:49:16Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"1119f104d121784215996a95900b40cda72326f4","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/djosh34/tigerstore/pulls/79/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/djosh34/tigerstore/pulls/79/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/djosh34/tigerstore/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/djosh34/tigerstore/issues/79/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/djosh34/tigerstore/statuses/1c0208a325b80d0a0ab4867748863ff24c1c6a36","head":{"label":"djosh34:work/50-hpack","ref":"work/50-hpack","sha":"1c0208a325b80d